  "extractionNotes": "Grant evidenced only by a ZUS note (maternity benefit granted) next to a register extract; no dates or rate printed by ZUS, so all periods are the claim (employee's leave application of 2026-03-16 and the Z-3 span 2026-02-26..2027-03-10: 140 + 14 + 224 = 378 days, 54 weeks). Child born at 36 completed weeks, 2640 g, discharged and re-admitted 2026-03-04..2026-03-13 (10 days) on the new-template certificate -> 2 weeks of supplementary leave. The leave application (18 days after birth) covers the whole leave, so 81.5% is inferred; supplementary assumed at 100%. After a phone call from ZUS the claimant wrote that the father will use his own pool at the same time while she uses her whole leave herself; his periods are not given. She also wrote that maternity benefit is due from only one workplace (single-title statement); the register extract shows a second, greyed-out row that is not legible. Quarter-time employment since 2022-10-01; Z-3 salary 1075.00 (2024-08..12) and 1166.50 (2025-01..07), a quarter of the minimum wage, so a low base and a likely top-up (not documented). The salary table ends in 2025-07 although the birth is in 2026-02, which suggests a base carried over from an earlier incapacity that is not in the file; months kept as printed. Column 6 is the contractual amount; contributionBase inferred equal to it. Employer marked up to 20 insured. asOf = leave application / Z-3 application date (ZUS note undated)."
